# Gentoo package catalogue for this workstation.
#
#   group | atom (category/name) | repo | tier | note
#
# repo   : ::gentoo  = official tree
#          hyproverlay / guru = overlay that must be enabled first (see below)
# tier   : required | recommended | optional
#
# Atom names verified against the official tree, ::guru and ::hyproverlay
# (2026-09). No versions are pinned. This file is data only — `install.sh deps`
# reports on it and prints commands; it never runs emerge.
#
# Overlays used here:
#   hyproverlay  https://codeberg.org/hyproverlay/hyproverlay
#                Hyprland stack (fast-moving; recommended by the Gentoo wiki)
#     enable:  eselect repository enable hyproverlay && emaint sync -r hyproverlay
#     keywords: echo '*/*::hyproverlay' > /etc/portage/package.accept_keywords/hyproverlay
#   guru         https://github.com/gentoo/guru  (community overlay)
#                Quickshell, brightnessctl, wev, wlr-randr
#     enable:  eselect repository enable guru && emaint sync -r guru
#     keywords: per-package ~amd64 in /etc/portage/package.accept_keywords/

# ---- base / common --------------------------------------------------------
base | app-shells/bash                | ::gentoo    | required    |
base | app-misc/jq                    | ::gentoo    | required    | used by the Infinite Desktop scripts
base | dev-vcs/git                    | ::gentoo    | required    |
base | dev-python/evdev               | ::gentoo    | required    | Infinite Desktop evdev daemon (python-evdev)
base | sys-apps/pciutils              | ::gentoo    | required    | lspci, used by install.sh check/doctor
base | sys-process/procps             | ::gentoo    | required    | ps, used by hardware detection
base | app-eselect/eselect-repository | ::gentoo    | required    | needed to enable the overlays below
base | app-portage/cpuid2cpuflags     | ::gentoo    | recommended | derive CPU_FLAGS_X86 for make.conf

# ---- Hyprland ------------------------------------------------------------
# gui-wm/hyprland MUST be built with USE="X systemd dbus-session":
#   X            -> Xwayland / X11 app support (pulls x11-base/xwayland)
#   systemd      -> systemd user-session integration (graphical-session.target)
#   dbus-session -> D-Bus session bus (portals, mako, hyprpolkitagent)
# All three are default USE on the default/linux/amd64/23.0/desktop/systemd
# profile this repo targets, so a stock desktop/systemd install needs no
# package.use entry. `doctor` verifies the built flags. See docs/SESSION.md.
hyprland | gui-wm/hyprland                      | hyproverlay | required    | compositor. Needs USE="X systemd dbus-session" (see comment above).
hyprland | x11-base/xwayland                    | ::gentoo    | required    | X11 app support; pulled by gui-wm/hyprland[X]. Listed so deps/doctor verify it survived a rebuild.
hyprland | gui-libs/xdg-desktop-portal-hyprland | hyproverlay | required    | portal backend: screencast / screenshot / global-shortcuts (wlroots screencopy + PipeWire)
hyprland | sys-apps/xdg-desktop-portal          | ::gentoo    | required    | portal frontend (org.freedesktop.portal.Desktop)
hyprland | sys-apps/xdg-desktop-portal-gtk      | ::gentoo    | required    | portal backend for the file chooser + Settings — needed by Chromium/Electron/Flatpak "Open File" dialogs
hyprland | sys-auth/polkit                      | ::gentoo    | required    | privilege prompts (the polkit daemon)
hyprland | sys-auth/hyprpolkitagent             | hyproverlay | required    | polkit *agent* that renders the prompts; lua/autostart.lua starts its systemd user unit hyprpolkitagent.service. Replaces a manual polkit-gnome/-kde agent.
hyprland | gui-apps/foot                        | ::gentoo    | required    | terminal: lua/bindings.lua's Super+Return runs $TERMINAL, falling back to `foot`. Set $TERMINAL + install that instead if you prefer another.
hyprland | gui-apps/hyprpaper                   | hyproverlay | optional    | wallpaper daemon
hyprland | gui-apps/hyprpicker                  | hyproverlay | optional    | colour picker

# ---- Quickshell (this project uses Quickshell, not Waybar) ---------------
quickshell | gui-apps/quickshell | guru | required | the bar / shell

# ---- notifications -----------------------------------------------------
# Wayland notification daemon. Owns the D-Bus name org.freedesktop.Notifications
# (session, activatable) — without it, every app that calls notify-send / the
# Notifications API fails silently. Config: config/mako/config (linked by
# `install.sh dotfiles`); autostarted by config/hypr/lua/autostart.lua.
notifications | gui-apps/mako     | ::gentoo | required    | notification daemon (org.freedesktop.Notifications)
notifications | x11-libs/libnotify | ::gentoo | recommended | provides notify-send — the CLI that lets scripts (e.g. hypr-screenshot) actually deliver a notification to mako

# ---- desktop utilities (launcher, clipboard, screenshots) ---------------
# The everyday tools that make a clean install usable. fuzzel is the launcher
# (Super+Space); wl-clipboard is the base Wayland clipboard (wl-copy/wl-paste),
# also used by the region screenshot; grim+slurp back bin/hypr-screenshot
# (Print / Super+Shift+S / Super+Print). See docs/INSTALL.md and README.
desktop-utils | gui-apps/fuzzel       | guru     | required | app launcher (Super+Space). Config: config/fuzzel/fuzzel.ini. guru overlay: add `gui-apps/fuzzel ~amd64` to /etc/portage/package.accept_keywords/
desktop-utils | gui-apps/wl-clipboard | ::gentoo | required | wl-copy / wl-paste — Wayland clipboard; the region screenshot copies the image with wl-copy
desktop-utils | gui-apps/grim         | ::gentoo | required | screenshot capture (bin/hypr-screenshot)
desktop-utils | gui-apps/slurp        | ::gentoo | required | region selector for grim (Super+Shift+S)

# ---- fonts (avoid tofu on a minimal install) ---------------------------
# No repo config names a font family — mako/fuzzel/foot/hyprlock/Quickshell all
# use the fontconfig aliases `sans-serif` / `monospace`. Something must back
# those aliases. dejavu is the small, stable, zero-keyword baseline; noto adds
# broad Unicode + a colour-emoji font. `doctor` checks `fc-match`.
fonts | media-fonts/dejavu     | ::gentoo | required    | sans/serif/mono baseline for the `sans-serif` / `monospace` fontconfig aliases
fonts | media-fonts/noto       | ::gentoo | recommended | broad Unicode coverage (Noto Sans/Serif/Mono). ~amd64: add `media-fonts/noto ~amd64` to /etc/portage/package.accept_keywords/
fonts | media-fonts/noto-emoji | ::gentoo | recommended | colour emoji — no repo config uses emoji glyphs, but notifications / web content do. ~amd64.

# ---- audio (PipeWire) ---------------------------------------------------
# Install AND enable the user units — they are socket-activated, not started
# by anything in this repo:  systemctl --user enable --now pipewire.socket
#   pipewire-pulse.socket wireplumber.service   (no root; see docs/SESSION.md).
# `install.sh first-run --apply` offers to run that; `doctor` checks it.
audio | media-video/pipewire    | ::gentoo | required    | audio server. Enable USE pipewire-pulse (PulseAudio API — Firefox/Discord/…) + alsa-plugin.
audio | media-video/wireplumber | ::gentoo | required    | PipeWire session/policy manager (wireplumber.service)
audio | sys-auth/rtkit          | ::gentoo | recommended | realtime scheduling for PipeWire — smoother audio under load (pipewire uses it over D-Bus if present)

# ---- network ----------------------------------------------------------
network | net-misc/networkmanager     | ::gentoo | required    |
network | sys-kernel/linux-firmware   | ::gentoo | required    | MediaTek MT7921 Wi-Fi firmware (mt7921e)
network | net-wireless/wireless-regdb | ::gentoo | recommended | Wi-Fi regulatory database
network | net-wireless/iw             | ::gentoo | optional    | Wi-Fi debugging

# ---- laptop / power / idle -------------------------------------------
power | gui-apps/hypridle      | hyproverlay | required    | idle -> dim / lock / dpms / suspend
power | gui-apps/hyprlock      | hyproverlay | required    | screen locker
power | sys-power/upower       | ::gentoo    | required    | battery / AC state over D-Bus (org.freedesktop.UPower, system-activated); Quickshell modules/Battery.qml. Default USE is enough.
power | app-misc/brightnessctl | guru        | required    | backlight control for the media keybinds
power | media-sound/playerctl  | ::gentoo    | recommended | MPRIS media keys
power | sys-power/powertop     | ::gentoo    | optional    | read-only power-draw diagnostics
power | gui-apps/wev           | guru        | optional    | first-run only: print real XF86 keysyms (docs/FIRST-RUN.md), not a runtime dep of lua/laptop.lua

# wpctl (used by lua/laptop.lua's volume/mute binds) is WirePlumber's own CLI
# and ships inside media-video/wireplumber above — no separate atom.

# ---- NVIDIA (compute / CUDA / OptiX; not the desktop GPU) -----------
nvidia | x11-drivers/nvidia-drivers   | ::gentoo | required    | also ships nvidia-persistenced
nvidia | dev-util/nvidia-cuda-toolkit | ::gentoo | optional    | CUDA (AI/ML, compute)
nvidia | dev-libs/cudnn               | ::gentoo | optional    | cuDNN for deep-learning frameworks

# ---- kernel / compiler / systems development ----------------------
kernel-dev | sys-kernel/gentoo-sources | ::gentoo | required    | kernel source (NOT vendored into this repo)
kernel-dev | sys-kernel/linux-headers  | ::gentoo | required    |
kernel-dev | dev-build/make            | ::gentoo | required    |
kernel-dev | sys-devel/gcc             | ::gentoo | required    | usually already in @system
kernel-dev | sys-devel/binutils        | ::gentoo | required    |
kernel-dev | sys-devel/bc              | ::gentoo | required    | kernel build
kernel-dev | sys-devel/flex            | ::gentoo | required    | kernel build
kernel-dev | sys-devel/bison           | ::gentoo | required    | kernel build
kernel-dev | sys-libs/ncurses          | ::gentoo | required    | make menuconfig
kernel-dev | sys-apps/kmod             | ::gentoo | required    | module tooling
kernel-dev | app-arch/cpio             | ::gentoo | required    | initramfs
kernel-dev | dev-util/pahole           | ::gentoo | recommended | BTF debug info for modern kernels
kernel-dev | dev-debug/gdb             | ::gentoo | recommended |
kernel-dev | dev-debug/strace          | ::gentoo | recommended |
kernel-dev | dev-util/ccache           | ::gentoo | optional    | speed up rebuilds
kernel-dev | dev-util/perf             | ::gentoo | optional    | profiling (tracks your kernel version)
kernel-dev | sys-apps/kexec-tools      | ::gentoo | optional    | fast reboot into a test kernel
kernel-dev | llvm-core/clang           | ::gentoo | optional    | Clang-built kernels / eBPF
kernel-dev | llvm-core/llvm            | ::gentoo | optional    |
kernel-dev | llvm-core/lld             | ::gentoo | optional    | LLVM linker for LLVM=1 builds
kernel-dev | sys-devel/sparse          | ::gentoo | recommended | make C=1/C=2 CHECK=sparse static analysis
kernel-dev | dev-libs/elfutils         | ::gentoo | recommended | libelf — objtool/resolve_btfids/perf need it
kernel-dev | dev-libs/openssl          | ::gentoo | recommended | module/kernel signing, certs (usually already in @system)
kernel-dev | dev-lang/rust             | ::gentoo | optional    | Rust-for-Linux + general Rust work
kernel-dev | dev-build/cmake           | ::gentoo | optional    | C/C++ projects
kernel-dev | dev-build/ninja           | ::gentoo | optional    | C/C++ projects
kernel-dev | app-emulation/qemu        | ::gentoo | optional    | boot-test kernels in a VM

# perl (dev-lang/perl) and python (dev-lang/python) are not listed as their
# own atoms above: both are part of Gentoo's @system set already on any
# profile this repo targets, so there is nothing for install.sh deps to add.
# install.sh kernel-dev --check still verifies both are actually on PATH,
# since Kconfig and scripts/checkpatch.pl/get_maintainer.pl/gen_compile_commands.py
# need them at runtime, not at merge time.
